# Day 5 – Permissions 
    
# What I Learned
  - Understood the permission string

  - change and view permissions for files and folders
  
# Commands Practiced
  -`chmod *** file_name` or forlder name
  - `ls -l`
  - `ls -ld`
  
# What I Understood in Simple Words
  -For Permission string
  - rwx = 7
  - rw- = 6
  - r-x = 5
  - r-- = 4 and so on
    - read(r)-> 4
    - write(w)-> 2
    - execute(x)-> 1
  -change permission with chmod for both files and folders
  - for ex: `- rwxrw-r-x` (permission 765) means
    - first part rwx=7 is for owner
    - 2nd part rw- = 6 is for group
    - 3rd part r-x = 5 is for others
  
# Problems I Faced
  -Couldn't understand what r, w, x for folders mean
# How I Fixed Them
  - r means you can read the things inside a folder
  - w means you can create, delete and change things inside a folder
  - x means whether you can enter the said forlder
